Add battery energy management from pack voltage

The INA219 cannot see motor current (its shunt handles ~3.2 A and the ESCs
bypass it), so energy management is derived from the pack voltage, which
is the metric that actually reflects a LiPo's state of charge.

- safety/battery: pure module with the LiPo discharge curve. Provides
  cell voltage, state of charge, remaining mAh for a given pack capacity,
  and a level (OK / LOW -> land / CRITICAL -> cut).
- main: failsafe now uses CRITICAL for the motor cut and LOW for the
  advisory beep, instead of the previous inline threshold check. Invalid
  readings (below BATTERY_MIN_PLAUSIBLE_V) never trigger the failsafe.
- CLI "power" now reports cell voltage, SoC %, remaining mAh and level.
- OLED status view shows pack voltage, SoC % and remaining mAh.
- config: BATTERY_CAPACITY_MAH 1550 for the 4S pack.
- tests: new test_battery suite (23 checks) covering the curve, clamping,
  monotonicity, remaining capacity, level thresholds and the implausible
  reading case. Total 159 checks.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
